From: Liuqin Linux Kit contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve Liuqin device support on Linux 7.3

Port the existing board interfaces, device-tree data and tested behavior from
linux-sm8450-liuqin fe81794b5e1b8a3f11a165f3acbfdb8fa671dbb3 plus the Liuqin
Linux Kit target adaptations through CABC and battery telemetry. The previous
adapted source was 4c839421353d066382fde9c260703aa098519a41. File-level authorship
and licenses are retained.

The Iris platform layout follows Seeker0472/liuqin-nixos commit
73e8071e09880aeb47f0a427b9a65b8cc10927c4, pkgs/kernel/patches/0006-liuqin-media-iris.patch,
rebased to the current firmware-descriptor API. Do not infer hardware validation
from successful compilation. The existing installer and product lock stay on 6.17.

Newer mainline DPU, atomic-commit, panel allocation/follower, GPIO descriptor,
audio and UCSI APIs replace the corresponding old mechanisms. Preserve first-frame
backlight ordering, panel policies, FPC IRQ-level semantics, camera registers,
GPU reporting/recovery and battery units. Already-upstream DSI rounding and MDSS
SMMU fixes are not duplicated. Unrelated phone drivers and DTs are excluded.

This patch is a reviewable experimental baseline, to be split by subsystem after
hardware validation. No firmware or per-device calibration is included.

diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-class-backlight-ktz8866 b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-class-backlight-ktz8866
