@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+What:           /sys/class/backlight/ktz8866-backlight/brightness_curve
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        Liuqin Linux Kit contributors
+Description:    Read-only active scale: liuqin-oem or linear. The former maps
+                logical 0..4095 through the exact M81 ROM curve to raw 0..2047.
+
+What:           /sys/class/backlight/ktz8866-backlight/default_brightness
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        Liuqin Linux Kit contributors
+Description:    Read-only logical default corresponding to raw brightness 1500.
+
+What:           /sys/class/backlight/ktz8866-backlight/raw_brightness
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        Liuqin Linux Kit contributors
+Description:    Read-only programmed 11-bit brightness code. I2C errors propagate.
+
+What:           /sys/class/backlight/ktz8866-backlight/pwm_level
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        Liuqin Linux Kit contributors
+Description:    Read-only 11-bit PWM-to-digital measurement. I2C errors propagate.
+                Neither diagnostic attribute reads the read-to-clear FLAG byte.
diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-liuqin-cabc b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-liuqin-cabc
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..506114c4ce0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-liuqin-cabc
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+What:           /sys/bus/mipi-dsi/devices/.../cabc_mode
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        Liuqin Linux Kit <build@liuqin.invalid>
+Description:    Present only for recognized M81 panels. Root may write off, ui,
+                still, or movie. Shows the requested mode; unchanged means no
+                explicit policy has been requested since probe. An explicit
+                selection survives blanking, suspend and display recovery until
+                driver removal/reboot. Writes while blanked are deferred until
+                successful normal-display/first-frame setup. A failed transfer
+                returns its error and retains the request for an explicit retry
+                or the next enable cycle. There is no automatic retry loop.
+                Boot parameter panel_novatek_nt36532.oem_cabc=-1 (default) keeps
+                the existing ON-table/reset behavior; 0..3 select these modes.
+                The reset state and Android userspace default are not inferred.
+
+What:           /sys/bus/mipi-dsi/devices/.../cabc_status
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        Liuqin Linux Kit <build@liuqin.invalid>
+Description:    Read-only requested/programmed mode, enable cycle, readiness and
+                last transfer error. programmed records successful command
+                submission, not a hardware register readback. unknown is used
+                before explicit programming, after blanking or after a failed
+                transfer. Reading these attributes issues no DSI commands.
diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-liuqin-panel b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-liuqin-panel
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..cbaeb3106b9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-liuqin-panel
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+What:           /sys/bus/mipi-dsi/devices/*/esd_status
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        Liuqin Linux Kit contributors
+Description:    Read-only version=1 key/value record: available, enabled,
+                pending, armed (two-bit mask), cycle, events, last (0/1 IRQ,
+                2 privileged test), age_ms since completed first-frame setup.
+                POLLPRI notification announces a latched fault. Interrupts
+                remain masked until another successful display activation.
+                A line must first be sampled low before its high IRQ is armed.
+                No DCS read or display reset is performed in interrupt context.
+
+What:           /sys/bus/mipi-dsi/devices/*/esd_inject
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        Liuqin Linux Kit contributors
+Description:    Root-only write of 1 injects a software test event while active.
+                This does not write panel/voltage registers. The active display
+                session may act on the event by cycling its output power.
